# Rule - Realtime status (WIP)

Open the five process files through `{workspace}/artifacts-map.json`.

## When

Run a checkpoint while the current item is not Done: the user pauses, a meaningful step inside a WIP item finishes, a new on-going task (OGT), open defect, or open RID appears, or the user asks to sync process files.

Do not run this rule instead of [`sdd-dod.mdc`](./sdd-dod.mdc) on close.

## Write

Draft tier-1 and tier-2 updates only. Show the draft. Write after the user confirms.

Tier 1: `status.md` per `{client_root}/templates/framework.sdd.works/sdd-scrum-practices.md` `#statusmd`.

Tier 2: `issues-log.md` for open defects; `sprint-backlog.md` for WIP rows and Open RIDs only; `product-backlog.md` for PBI WIP only after the user confirmed that PBI is in progress.

Leave `changes-log.md` to DoD or an explicit user request to record a change.

bad example: mark the SBI Done on sprint-backlog during a checkpoint because the code looks finished.
good example: set the SBI row to WIP and refresh where we are now on status.md; leave Done to sdd-dod.mdc after confirm.

## Do not

Mark PBI, SBI, or sprint Done. Set sprint Status Done. Close an RID. Invent sprint, SBI, or OGT rows. Write without confirm.

Wording checks: [`friendly-language.mdc`](./friendly-language.mdc).
